<section id="comments">
  <h2>Comments (2)</h2>

  
    <a id="comment-8421" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0397#comment-8421">Comment #8421</a>
        by
        <cite>Ryo Suzuki</cite>
        on <time datetime="2023-05-23 22:12:50.944938">May 23, 2023 at 22:12 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>The proof can be simplified.</p>
<p>By virtue of  Lemma 01TH, it is sufficient to prove that:
Let <script type="math/tex">Y</script> be a locally Noetherian scheme, and <script type="math/tex">x \in Y</script>. Then <script type="math/tex">x</script> is isolated in <script type="math/tex">Y</script> if and only if <script type="math/tex">{\rm dim}_x Y=0</script>. </p>
<p>Proof. If <script type="math/tex">x</script> is an isolated point, <script type="math/tex">\{x\}</script> is open (by Definition 06RM). Hence {\rm dim}_x Y = 0 (by Definition 0055). Conversely, if <script type="math/tex">{\rm dim}_x(Y) =0</script>, then there exists an open subset <script type="math/tex">x\in U\subset Y</script> such that <script type="math/tex">{\rm dim} U = 0</script>. We can take <script type="math/tex">U</script> Noetherian because <script type="math/tex">Y</script> is locally Noetherian. Since <script type="math/tex">U</script> is 0-dimensional Noetherian scheme, it is discrete. Hence <script type="math/tex">x</script> is isolated point of <script type="math/tex">Y</script>. q.e.d.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  
    <a id="comment-9045" class="header-offset"></a>
    <article>
      <header>
        <p><a href="/tag/0397#comment-9045">Comment #9045</a>
        by
        <cite><a href="https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/" rel="author">Stacks project</a></cite>
        
        on <time datetime="2024-05-03 13:20:07.658782">May 03, 2024 at 13:20 </time>
      </header>

      <blockquote><p>Thanks very much. I decided to leave in the proof we have now and add yours as a second clearly shorter one. Changes are <a href="https://github.com/stacks/stacks-project/commit/e822d95f2f1d6f94d2d60e80008649e2ded8dcd6">here</a>.</p></blockquote>
    </article>
  

  
